<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell seven points to 1,287.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell seven points to 1,287.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,287 today from 1,294 on July 28, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1409    12.794	  1411    12.806</p>
<p>   1a   1277  9675.000	  1286  9738.000</p>
<p>   2    1571    22.450	  1566    22.375</p>
<p>   2a   1522 12481.000	  1529 12538.000</p>
<p>   3    1412    13.025	  1424    13.138</p>
<p>   3a   1127  8894.000	  1147  9050.000</p>
<p>   6    1275    13.150	  1276    13.156</p>
